      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly support the claim that “fighting” means “actively working against a disease through coordinated efforts …” as a definition of the term; it only uses “health organizations that are fighting” a disease in describing the study context, without defining “fighting.”",
        "The definition’s specific claims that the efforts are “aimed at reducing the disease’s impact” are not stated in the packet text provided (no direct description of reducing disease impact as the meaning of “fighting”).",
        "While the packet mentions “global health network partnerships,” “coordination,” “improving its resilience,” and “better health strategies,” it does not explicitly define “strengthening the network responding to it” as the sense of “fighting,” making that part of the definition partly inferential."
